  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through Sunday)\nIssued at 134 AM CDT Mon Oct 19 2026\n\nTuesday night we continue our warming pattern as broad ridging over \nSouth Central Texas becomes more amplified heading into the late \nweek period. Each day we will continue to warm until we eventually \njump back above normal for highs by Wednesday and continuing into \nthe weekend. This means we should see highs in the low to mid 80s \nbefore highs ramp up into the upper 80s to low 90s by the end of the \nweek. Additionally, we will see the return of more humid\nconditions for the upcoming weekend with dewpoints back into the \n50s and 60s compared to the dry 30s and 40s currently in place. \nEventually, a trough is progged to move over the western U.S late \nin the period but the elongated upper ridge could limit impacts \nfor most of our area associated with this feature. The exception \nbeing the Rio Grande and Southern Edwards Plateau regions where \njust enough of a disturbance could clip these areas late in the \nweekend. However, confidence remains pretty low as pops are only \nin the 20% range for now. Continue to check back as the forecast \nchanges and we may finally break this dry pattern we our currently\nlocked into.",
